From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:50:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add Rockchip command sequence panel driver

Add a driver for "rockchip,cmd-panel" panels: parallel RGB panels whose
controller is set up with command sequences sent over a 3-wire SPI link
with 9-bit words, bit-banged on GPIOs.

Everything is read from the device tree: the mode and bus flags from
display-timings (native mode) or panel-timing, the optional power
supply, enable and reset GPIOs, the power up delays, the init and exit
sequences in the Rockchip format, the backlight and the panel
orientation. The bus format defaults to RGB888_1X24.

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS                                |   6 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig              |  12 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-rockchip-cmd.c | 398 +++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 417 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-rockchip-cmd.c

